Literature for cycle 1 is in `runs/Absolute_2026-09-28_01/sota/cycle-001/literature-2.json`.

The source method is a camera-axis min/max span and a mean range on `/pps/pallet_pose_rich`. This pass lists other published ways to size the face with the same pose:

- Interquartile and occupancy-quantile boxes
- Covariance oriented boxes
- Rotating-calipers minimum-area rectangles
- Contour, line, and particle-filter dimensions
- Pallet-template edge matching
- Pocket width and height from a depth hint
- A percentile fit in place of the mean range

These do not replace the required camera-x span, camera-y span, and mean range. No evolve run was started, and the run was not scored.
